<p data-source-range="159:167">Components that already exposed their tokens at <code>:root</code> before this map — <code>.dc-alert</code>,
<code>.dc-skill-card</code> colors, <code>.dc-specialty-intro</code> colors, <code>.dc-path-shell</code> colors,
<code>.dc-specialty-card</code> colors, <code>.dc-block</code>, <code>.dc-section</code>, and the chapter-opener
composite — keep their existing public-API blocks in <code>dc-component-defaults.css</code>. A handful of
component-scoped tokens (e.g. <code>--dc-ap-bg</code>, <code>--dc-sidebar-accent</code>,
<code>--dc-fiction-bg</code>) are deliberately <em>not</em> in this map: they are assigned per
modifier/variant inside the component rule and have no single global default.</p>
</div>
<hr data-source-range="168:169">
<div class="section gp-columns-2 dc-column-panel" data-source-range="170:171"><h2>Font Size Token Notes</h2>
<div class="dc-alert dc-note"><span class="dc-alert-label">Note</span>
<p data-source-range="174:176">Pull quotes use <code>--fs-h2</code> directly. They are intentionally set at section-heading weight rather than a separate display scale.</p>
</div>
<div class="dc-alert dc-note"><span class="dc-alert-label">Note</span>
<p data-source-range="177:179">Chevron banners use <code>--fs-h1</code> directly. This keeps banner headings and body H1s on the same display scale.</p>
</div>
<h2>See It In Action</h2>
<p>These examples show the DC palette applied to real book pages using actual Dimm City Field Guide content.</p>
<ul>
<li data-source-range="184:185"><a href="#ch-example-front-matter" data-gp-source-token="[Front Matter &amp; TOC](#ch-example-front-matter)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Front Matter &amp; TOC</a> — cream paper and ink-dust on credits and TOC pages</li>
<li data-source-range="185:186"><a href="#ch-example-chapter-opener" data-gp-source-token="[Chapter Openers](#ch-example-chapter-opener)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Chapter Openers</a> — crimson chevron banners and brick-texture background in context</li>
<li data-source-range="186:187"><a href="#ch-example-specialty-overview" data-gp-source-token="[Specialty Overview](#ch-example-specialty-overview)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Specialty Overview</a> — specialty palette in action across intro pages</li>
<li data-source-range="187:188"><a href="#ch-example-specialty-profile" data-gp-source-token="[Specialty Profile](#ch-example-specialty-profile)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Specialty Profile</a> — fire palette on skill cards and spray banners</li>
<li data-source-range="188:189"><a href="#ch-example-rules" data-gp-source-token="[Rules &amp; Mechanics](#ch-example-rules)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Rules &amp; Mechanics</a> — HUD blue on outcome tables and roll chips</li>
<li data-source-range="189:190"><a href="#ch-example-dm-npcs" data-gp-source-token="[Dream Master Pages](#ch-example-dm-npcs)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Dream Master Pages</a> — amber warnings and ink-smoke secondary text</li>
<li data-source-range="190:192"><a href="#ch-example-gear-tech" data-gp-source-token="[Gear &amp; Tech](#ch-example-gear-tech)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0">Gear &amp; Tech</a> — fire-palette rules tables and cybernetics reference</li>
</ul>
<div class="dc-alert dc-note"><span class="dc-alert-label">Note</span>
<p data-source-range="192:194"><strong>Ink coverage cap:</strong> Keep total CMYK coverage under 280 % for coated stock and under 240 % for uncoated. Saturated fire palette colors run high — request a physical proof before full print run.</p>
</div>
</div></div></div>"
